WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.047 --> 00:00:05.828
Ray's Diner was packed.

2
00:00:05.829 --> 00:00:11.071
The Food Truck Rally episode filmed in Sandville was finally airing on TV.

3
00:00:11.072 --> 00:00:16.160
Everyone's gaze was glued to the big screen where the show was streaming.

4
00:00:16.161 --> 00:00:18.636
Everyone's except for Ally's.

5
00:00:18.637 --> 00:00:23.148
She was busy walking around the diner with a tray of cookies.

6
00:00:23.149 --> 00:00:27.414
"Would you like a cookie?" Ally asked, going from table to table.

7
00:00:27.415 --> 00:00:29.740
"Randy baked them."

8
00:00:29.741 --> 00:00:35.315
Soon the show returned from a commercial break.

9
00:00:35.316 --> 00:00:39.276
"What a great contest!" Mark Marx said on TV.

10
00:00:39.277 --> 00:00:41.543
"We've loved being in Sandville.

11
00:00:41.544 --> 00:00:43.394
What a friendly place.

12
00:00:43.395 --> 00:00:48.456
Except . . . it's the home of the world-famous UFO Museum.

13
00:00:48.457 --> 00:00:51.336
We wish we'd met at least one alien!"

14
00:00:51.337 --> 00:00:56.596
Laughter broke out both on TV and in the diner as the camera zoomed in on Ally.

15
00:00:56.597 --> 00:01:01.644
She wasn't laughing on TV, nor in real life, as Mark Marx went on.

16
00:01:01.645 --> 00:01:05.783
"And now the moment we've all be waiting for!"

17
00:01:05.784 --> 00:01:08.585
The diner grew silent.

18
00:01:08.586 --> 00:01:14.091
"Our winner is chosen not only for the quality of their food, but also for their persistence.

19
00:01:14.092 --> 00:01:17.509
We were impressed how Rolling Ray's never gave up.

20
00:01:17.510 --> 00:01:23.025
So impressed, in fact . . . you're our winners!"

21
00:01:23.026 --> 00:01:29.472
Mark Marx pulled the oversize check for five thousand dollars made out to Rolling Ray's from behind the curtain.

22
00:01:29.473 --> 00:01:32.126
"Come and collect your prize!"

23
00:01:32.127 --> 00:01:35.005
The diner customers cheered.

24
00:01:35.006 --> 00:01:39.735
"It's nice that our win is making other people happy too," Ally thought.

25
00:01:39.736 --> 00:01:45.440
A customer suddenly jumped up to applaud and hit Ally's tray, sending cookies flying.

26
00:01:45.441 --> 00:01:50.422
"Oh no!" Ally tried to activate her powers, but nothing happened.

27
00:01:50.423 --> 00:01:55.668
Ally groaned.

28
00:01:55.669 --> 00:01:58.775
"I miss my powers!" she thought.

29
00:01:58.776 --> 00:02:04.030
"Will I ever get them back?"

30
00:02:04.031 --> 00:02:07.752
Ray turned off the TV.

31
00:02:07.753 --> 00:02:10.987
"I'd like to make a toast to Barry and his team.

32
00:02:10.988 --> 00:02:13.153
I'm very proud of you all.

33
00:02:13.154 --> 00:02:16.275
Barry, we'll miss you while you're off at culinary school.

34
00:02:16.276 --> 00:02:17.281
But don't worry.

35
00:02:17.282 --> 00:02:20.600
Randy will take good care of Rolling Ray's."

36
00:02:20.601 --> 00:02:23.074
"Thank you." Barry blushed.

37
00:02:23.075 --> 00:02:25.264
"And thanks to the best team ever.

38
00:02:25.265 --> 00:02:31.039
I couldn't have done it without you!"

39
00:02:31.040 --> 00:02:34.619
*** Later Ally finished sweeping up the mess from the

40
00:02:34.620 --> 00:02:37.431
cookies. Mateo came over to help

41
00:02:37.432 --> 00:02:42.748
her. "I saw how upset you were about the cookies, but I couldn't get over fast enough to help

42
00:02:42.749 --> 00:02:46.424
you. Don't worry about it, Ally. They're just

43
00:02:46.425 --> 00:02:48.929
cookies." "It's not the cookies," Ally

44
00:02:48.930 --> 00:02:53.285
said. "It's my powers. I'm not me without them!"

45
00:02:53.286 --> 00:02:55.585
"I know," Mateo said.

46
00:02:55.586 --> 00:03:01.179
"And I'm sorry Alpha isn't working any better in the new phone you bought with your prize money."

47
00:03:01.180 --> 00:03:04.033
"Yep, she's still glitching."

48
00:03:04.034 --> 00:03:10.119
Ally sighed deeply as she pulled out her new phone.

49
00:03:10.120 --> 00:03:14.189
"Maybe you should buy a desktop computer," Mateo said.

50
00:03:14.190 --> 00:03:17.592
"It could be the only way to get Alpha to work again."

51
00:03:17.593 --> 00:03:21.831
"But then I can't carry Alpha around with me," Ally said.

52
00:03:21.832 --> 00:03:24.820
Julius and Kate came over.

53
00:03:24.821 --> 00:03:29.109
"I can't believe you're having trouble with your new phone too," Julius said.

54
00:03:29.110 --> 00:03:33.523
"How are we going to text and talk while I'm away at my grandma's house?"

55
00:03:33.524 --> 00:03:36.744
"You should exchange that phone, Ally," Kate said.

56
00:03:36.745 --> 00:03:39.367
"I'll go to the store with you tomorrow."

57
00:03:39.368 --> 00:03:42.143
"Kate cannot come with me!" Ally thought.

58
00:03:42.144 --> 00:03:46.075
"I have to remove Alpha and put her into any device I buy!"

59
00:03:46.076 --> 00:03:51.405
"Um . . . that's very nice of you, but I can go myself," Ally said.

60
00:03:51.406 --> 00:03:54.103
"Kate's a really good shopper," Julius said.

61
00:03:54.104 --> 00:03:55.542
"Why don't you take her along?

62
00:03:55.543 --> 00:03:58.269
She'll make sure you get the right replacement."

63
00:03:58.270 --> 00:04:02.462
"Okay, I guess. Sure," Ally mumbled.

64
00:04:02.463 --> 00:04:06.929
"I'd better go. I'm leaving early in the morning," Julius said.

65
00:04:06.930 --> 00:04:10.162
"I'll text you, Ally, when I arrive at my grandmother's."

66
00:04:10.163 --> 00:04:14.163
Everyone waved good-bye to Julius.

67
00:04:14.164 --> 00:04:17.256
"I'm going to miss him," Ally thought.

68
00:04:17.257 --> 00:04:22.427
"But I'm also going to be busy getting Alpha fixed and my powers back."

69
00:04:22.428 --> 00:04:24.953
Kate smiled at Mateo and Ally.

70
00:04:24.954 --> 00:04:30.424
"You two can keep each other company while both Julius and Bethany are out of town."

71
00:04:30.425 --> 00:04:34.904
Mateo nodded. "Bethany will be back from vacation soon.

72
00:04:34.905 --> 00:04:37.591
But Julius will be gone the whole month."

73
00:04:37.592 --> 00:04:42.243
"That's why you have to exchange that phone, Ally," Kate said.

74
00:04:42.244 --> 00:04:46.432
"I'll meet you at Everything Mart tomorrow morning at ten! Bye!"

75
00:04:46.433 --> 00:04:49.453
Ally waited for Kate to leave.

76
00:04:49.454 --> 00:04:53.757
"I guess I have no choice but to go with Kate to the store."

77
00:04:53.758 --> 00:04:59.756
Mateo laughed. "Nothing gets between Kate and the chance to shop!

78
00:04:59.757 --> 00:05:06.513
Speaking of shopping, I've got to get home to check the online auction for the first Cosmic Quest comic.

79
00:05:06.514 --> 00:05:09.201
So far, I'm the highest bidder.

80
00:05:09.202 --> 00:05:12.347
I want that comic so badly!"

81
00:05:12.348 --> 00:05:14.688
"Good luck!" Ally said.

82
00:05:14.689 --> 00:05:21.588
"I wish getting my powers back was as easy as bidding in an auction," she thought.

